WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.068
 Brendan and Cody,
congratulations.

00:00:03.168 --> 00:00:04.937
You guys are in the
third and final round

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.539
of this competition.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.108
Now when you came here, we asked
you to make smatchets to very

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.210
exacting specifications.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:15.048
Well, that's led us up to our
next and final challenge where

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:18.050
you'll have to forge this
parameter-heavy blade

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:23.523
from history, the Spanish
conquistador sword.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:27.226
Good luck.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.528
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.096
 Good luck, man.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.268
BRENDAN: So it's day one.

00:00:36.368 --> 00:00:38.504
We are in Atascadero,
California, at my home forge,

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:43.910
and I'm about to make a Spanish
conquistador sword from 80CrV2.

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:46.012
And so it begins.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.680
No power hammer, no press.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.050
I am just going to be doing
a lot of hammering today.

00:00:51.116 --> 00:00:53.219
It's got a lot of
parameters on it.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.389
It's got a knuckle
guard, medallion pummel,

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.425
a lot of places
that I can mess up.

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:02.161
So at this point at the end of
day one I moved a lot of metal,

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.430
and I did it without
a power hammer.

00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:10.269 line:0%
My hand doesn't really feel
very good, but it's all good.

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:11.604 line:0%
CODY: It's the
start of day three.

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.473
Today's going to be
all about the guard.

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.608
With all these
pieces on this guard,

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.478
the balance and the weight of
this is going to be an issue.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:21.681
Most of it's just going to
be seeming what feels right.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:25.952
I have to start bending up the
quillons and the knuckle-bow.

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:27.887
At first it was pretty
confusing trying

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:31.491
to figure out which direction
the swoops of the quillons

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.625
were supposed to go.

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:36.396
As I broke it down, it
became clear in my head.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.565
Starting to look like something.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:41.400
I have a big chunk of Damascus
left over from the blade

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.402
that I plan on using
for the pommel,

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:47.473
and this will balance out
the weight of the sword.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.409
I'm really happy with the
way everything came out,

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:51.744
so tomorrow will just be
a little bit of cleaning,

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.247
fine tuning, and shaping.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.148 line:7%
BRENDAN: Day three.

00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:57.950
I have to finish this blade.

00:01:58.016 --> 00:01:59.318
I got to get it heat treated.

00:01:59.418 --> 00:02:01.987
I got to get as much of
that done today as possible.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:04.423
So I got to get all
of that done today.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.459
As I'm forging this
thing out, I'm just about

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:09.762
done straightening it,
and I noticed that it's

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.164
not quite getting as hot.

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:14.000
The propane is running out.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.402
It's just slowly dropping.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.438
It's not very easy
to go fill this tank.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:21.474
At this point, I am
running out of time,

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:24.877
so I'm not going to quench today
because I won't be able to get

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:26.479
the blade hot enough.

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:29.648 line:0%
So I'm going to just wait it
out until I have the propane,

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:32.285 line:0%
get the even heat that
I need because there's

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:35.320 line:7%
zero room for error.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.890 line:0%
CODY: It's the
start of day four.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.791
I have to get
everything cleaned up.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.660
I've got to get
the handle shaped.

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.662
I will bed it with epoxy.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:46.566
I'm going to wax the tang and
then pour it into the handle,

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:49.168
and that will set up.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:51.337
I think I can afford to
do a little texturing.

00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:54.207
It'll add a little bit of grip.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:56.776
Everything slides on
just as I want them too.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:59.979 line:7%
This thing will KEAL.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.714 line:0%
BRENDAN: So it's
day four, last day.

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:04.050 line:0%
I was able to get some
new propane in the tank.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:06.285
I have a big list of
stuff to do today.

00:03:06.351 --> 00:03:10.990
So I'm quenching before
I do anything else.

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.259
Yeah, it came out great.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:17.129
Now I have to start thinking
about all the other components

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.598
of this build.

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:21.534
Starting out with this guard,
I'm actually welding it

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.969
to the blade
because I won't have

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:25.071
to worry about it slipping off.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.606
I think it'll be fine.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.508
I'm checking the specs, and
it says disk-shaped pommel.

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:31.411
It doesn't say that
it has to be steel.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:35.782
So I think that my best bet is
just making one out of wood.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:36.715
It's over.

00:03:36.782 --> 00:03:37.850
I'm tired.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:40.619
I am stoked that I think
I hit every parameter,

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:45.258
and I feel extremely excited
to see this thing in action.

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:49.028
 All right, bladesmiths,
welcome to the KEAL test.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.030
Your weapons are lovely,
but are they deadly?

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.965
Well, to find out, I
will take your weapon,

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:57.169
deliver some slashes and thrusts
on this beautiful Spanish goat.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:58.104
Cody, you're up first.

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:58.938
You ready for this?

00:03:59.005 --> 00:04:00.172
I'm ready.

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:04.244
[music playing]

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:22.895
 All right, Cody,
I think there's

00:04:22.961 --> 00:04:24.897
a little bit of a problem here.

00:04:24.998 --> 00:04:28.000
I can't get my eyes past
the beauty of the Damascus

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.001
that you have right here.

00:04:29.101 --> 00:04:30.802
This is a beautiful piece.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.071
It cuts deeply.

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:34.573
It thrusts nicely even
when hitting bone,

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:36.708
and it is a pleasure to wield.

00:04:36.775 --> 00:04:38.911
Sure is a beautiful
sword that you have here.

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:39.945
It will KEAL.

00:04:40.045 --> 00:04:41.614
 Yeah.

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:43.015
 All right, Brendan,
your turn, sir.

00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:43.949
Time to have fun?

00:04:44.049 --> 00:04:44.784
 Yeah.

00:04:44.851 --> 00:04:45.817
 Let's do this.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:49.756
[music playing]

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.674
 Good job.

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:11.177
 All right, Brendan, let's
talk about your sword here.

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:13.078
Your blade did
take a little bend

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:14.313
here that wasn't there earlier.

00:05:14.413 --> 00:05:16.749
The handle kind of
kicks up right now.

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.818
Now your edge is very
sharp right here.

00:05:19.918 --> 00:05:22.354
The point is sharp enough
to thrust all the weight.

00:05:22.454 --> 00:05:25.657
Using this edge delivers
that kind of cut.

00:05:25.724 --> 00:05:28.728
Overall, sir, your
weapon, it will KEAL.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:38.237
 Bladesmiths, welcome to
the perfect strength test

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:41.673
for your swords, our flex test.

00:05:41.773 --> 00:05:43.542
Now a properly
heat-treated blade will

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.577
bend and come back to true.

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:47.613
If it's not properly
heat treated,

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.283
it could bend, stay that way,
or just break altogether.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:52.785
Cody, you ready to go?

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:53.553
 Let's do it.

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.672
 Cody, really nice job.

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:13.305
Great balance.

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:14.306
Beautiful sword.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:15.174
It hasn't moved at all.

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:16.409
It's dead straight.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:18.477
Heat treating
Damascus on a knife

00:06:18.543 --> 00:06:20.179
can be tricky enough
sometimes, and doing it

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:22.281
on a sword like this
and keeping that heat

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:24.350
treat dead on, really nice job.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.685
 Thank you.

00:06:25.751 --> 00:06:27.753
 All right, Brendan,
you saw what's it like.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:28.855
How you feeling?

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:29.589
 A little nervous.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.480
 Good job, Brendan.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.483
Now you could see when it was
locked in the vice the guard

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.952
was kicked off to the
side, so you've got a twist

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:01.587
in your blade up at the tip.

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:04.056
You had a little bit of
a warp on the tip before.

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:07.293
It's a little bit further
now but not extreme.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:08.594
Good choice on the steels.

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:10.829
A little bit of a bend
but very good job.

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:11.564
 Thanks.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:18.337
 All right, bladesmiths,
now it's time to find

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:19.672
out how sharp your weapons are.

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:23.242
This is the sharpness
test, the fine slice.

00:07:23.342 --> 00:07:25.511
Now conquistador, or
conqueror in English,

00:07:25.611 --> 00:07:28.347
didn't just have to conquer
their enemies but the terrain

00:07:28.448 --> 00:07:30.616
that they find themselves
holding their weapon.

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:32.218
To find out how sharp
your weapons are,

00:07:32.284 --> 00:07:35.554
I will take your swords and
try to cut through these vines.

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:36.922
Now unlike the
strength test, this

00:07:37.022 --> 00:07:39.592
is all about how well
the edge of your blade

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:40.926
cuts through these vines.

00:07:41.026 --> 00:07:41.861
Cody, you're up first.

00:07:41.928 --> 00:07:42.394
You ready for this?

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:43.862
 Let's do it.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:47.800
[music playing]

00:08:03.782 --> 00:08:06.719
 All right, Cody, we
know from the KEAL test

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:09.955
the first 4 inches are sharp,
but now for the sharpness test

00:08:10.055 --> 00:08:14.126
the rest of the blade is
very sharp like a hot knife

00:08:14.193 --> 00:08:15.160
through butter.

00:08:15.227 --> 00:08:16.995
It will cut.

00:08:17.062 --> 00:08:18.864
All right, Brendan, your turn.
You ready, sir?

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:19.431
 Oh yeah.

00:08:19.498 --> 00:08:23.002
[music playing]

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:44.290
 All right, Brendan, let's
talk about your edge here.

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:46.125
The first 4 inches
here are very sharp,

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:47.993
this razor edge right there.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:51.464
Then it doesn't hold an edge on
any of these parts right here,

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:54.700
and then it picks up a sharp
edge in this area here.

00:08:54.766 --> 00:08:56.035
On that one vine it didn't cut.

00:08:56.101 --> 00:08:58.070
There is a laceration
but not deep enough.

00:08:58.137 --> 00:09:02.340
But on the areas that are
sharp, it cuts right through.

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:03.809
So it will cut.

00:09:06.745 --> 00:09:09.781
 All right, bladesmiths,
the "Forged in Fire" champion

00:09:09.848 --> 00:09:15.254
is Cody.

00:09:15.321 --> 00:09:16.555
Congratulations.

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:17.924
You're the new "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.926
Good job, brother.

00:09:20.026 --> 00:09:23.162
Brendan, unfortunately your
blade didn't make the cut.

00:09:23.262 --> 00:09:25.464
Come on forward, my friend.

00:09:25.531 --> 00:09:26.765
Good job, man.

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:28.500
BRENDAN: This was a very
difficult challenge.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:31.537
Having such a complex
final build to make,

00:09:31.603 --> 00:09:34.574
it was pretty crazy,
but it was a great time.

00:09:37.342 --> 00:09:38.511
 Cody, congratulations.

00:09:38.611 --> 00:09:40.112
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:43.315
and that's a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:44.416
Good job, my friend.

00:09:44.516 --> 00:09:46.986
[applause]

00:09:47.886 --> 00:09:49.521
 I just won "Forged in Fire."

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:51.257
This is awesome.

00:09:51.357 --> 00:09:53.225
This is the most
money I've ever had

00:09:53.291 --> 00:09:55.227
in one check, that's for sure.

00:09:55.294 --> 00:09:57.029
I have no idea what I'm
going to do with this money.

00:09:57.129 --> 00:09:58.964
I'm going to spend
some of it on my shop,

00:09:59.064 --> 00:10:01.266
and I'm going to spend
some of it on my family.

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:04.737
[music playing]

